ct form. Toast confirmed success and tag appeared in admin grid immediately, but the live product detail page (/product/sony-wh-1000xm5) after a fresh navigation still showed only the original 4 tags with no 'qa-tested' tag added or persisted anywhere (search/tag filters on /products also do not surface it).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Persistence bug: featured flag on newly created product does not persist\", \"actual\": \"Created 'QA Test Blender 3000' with Featured=true via the admin form. Because the create operation itself does not persist (see FT-1), the featured flag never reached the homepage Featured section, /products, or /category/home — the product disappeared entirely on reload, so its featured status could never be verified as displayed.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Persistence bug: edits to product spec/price/rating fields do not persist to storefront\", \"actual\": \"Editing Sony WH-1000XM5's price via the admin Edit form updated the admin grid instantly (399->379) but the change never reached the live product detail page, which continued to show the original $399 after a fresh page load, confirming edits are not written to the data store consumed by the storefront.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No dedicated tag categorization mechanism; also blocked by persistence bug\", \"actual\": \"The admin Create/Edit Product forms only expose a free-text tags field (comma-separated) with no mechanism to browse existing tags, categorize/group tags, or manage a tag taxonomy separately from a product. Additionally, any tag changes made do not persist past a page reload (same root cause as FT-4), so tag management is non-functional end-to-end.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category dropdown filter on /products and direct navigation to /category/tech, /category/home, /category/fitness each correctly showed only products belonging to the selected category, with counts matching expectations (e.g., /category/home showed exactly 3 Home products).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/products page displays the full catalog (9 products found with no filters applied), each rendered as a card with image, name, category, price, and rating, confirming complete browsing of all products without pagination gaps.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Verified minimum-rating filter (4.5+) correctly excluded Philips Hue Starter Kit (4.4 rating) while retaining qualifying products. Verified 'Price: Low to High' sort correctly ordered products ascending by price (e.g., Sony, then Samsung, then MacBook). Price range slider (native slider role) adjusts min threshold in $10 increments via ArrowRight/ArrowLeft and updates product count in real time.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category dropdown on /products and homepage browse-by-category cards expose exactly 3 verticals: Tech, Home, Fitness — no additional or missing categories found anywhere in the UI.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combined category + minimum-rating filter (e.g., Home + 4.5+) returned only products strictly satisfying both criteria; no out-of-range or mismatched-category items appeared in any tested filter/sort combination (rating filter, category filter, price sort).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changing search text, category dropdown, rating dropdown, sort order, and price slider all updated the product list and result count immediately without any page reload or loading spinner delay.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking a product card from /products or homepage navigated to its detail page (e.g., /product/dyson-v15-detect) instantly via client-side SPA routing, with no full page reload observed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Inspected the 'Buy Now' external retailer link via DOM evaluation on the Dyson V15 Detect product page: href='https://example.com/dyson-v15', target='_blank', rel='noopener noreferrer' — correct external link security pattern and functional href present.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Product detail pages (Dyson V15 Detect, Sony WH-1000XM5) fully displayed category, rating, price, Buy Now retailer link, tags, Key Specifications section, My Review text, and related 'More in [Category]' products — no truncation or missing sections observed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Existing catalog products are accurately categorized (e.g., Home category page shows only home-goods items) and tagged with relevant, descriptive tags visible consistently on both /products cards and individual product detail pages.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Data inconsistency between admin view and public views due to persistence bug\", \"actual\": \"After editing Sony WH-1000XM5 price and tags in admin, the admin grid showed the new values ($379, +qa-tested tag) while the public product detail page simultaneously showed the old, unmodified values ($399, original tags) — core content is inconsistent across views because admin changes never propagate to the underlying data store.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
